= ImdbProject =

'''ImdbProject''' is an automated test suite that checks the behaviour of the live [https://www.imdb.com IMDb] website. It is written as Behaviour-Driven Development (BDD) scenarios with [https://cucumber.io Cucumber] and drives a real web browser with [https://www.selenium.dev Selenium].

== Overview ==
The suite lives in the <code>hellocucumber</code> folder. Plain-English feature files describe what a visitor should be able to do on IMDb; step definitions turn each line into browser actions through page objects; and the results are written to an HTML report.

* '''Language and build:''' Java 17, Maven
* '''Libraries:''' Cucumber 7, Selenium 4, JUnit 5 (JUnit Platform Suite), PicoContainer
* '''Browsers:''' Google Chrome (default), Firefox and Safari
* '''Driver setup:''' none needed; Selenium Manager downloads a matching browser driver automatically

== What is tested ==
=== Top 250 Movies chart (<code>top_rated_movies.feature</code>) ===
{| class="wikitable"
! Scenario !! What it checks
|-
| Refining the list by genre || Choosing ''Comedy'', ''Action'' or ''Drama'' opens IMDb's search filtered by that genre, and it returns titles
|-
| Sorting by release date || After sorting by release date, ascending or descending, all 250 movies are listed in that order of release year
|}

=== Movie title page (<code>title_display_page.feature</code>) ===
The movie is set in configuration (default: ''The Shawshank Redemption'', <code>tt0111161</code>). All automated scenarios run while signed out.
{| class="wikitable"
! Scenario !! What it checks
|-
| Add to Watchlist || A signed-out visitor is sent to the sign-in page
|-
| Rate the movie (1 and 10 stars) || A signed-out visitor is sent to the sign-in page
|-
| Share on social media || The share menu offers Facebook, Twitter and Email, each linking to this movie
|-
| Copy a link || Choosing ''Copy link'' shows the message "Link copied"
|}

=== Manual scenarios ===
Creating an account and signing in with IMDb, Amazon, Facebook or Google need real accounts, CAPTCHAs and 2-step verification. They are kept in the feature file as documentation, tagged <code>@manual</code>, and skipped in automated runs.

The project also contains Cucumber's "Is it Friday yet?" tutorial (8 scenarios) as a simple example.

== How it works ==
* '''Feature files''' (<code>src/test/resources/imdbTests</code>) describe the behaviour in Gherkin (''Given / When / Then'').
* '''Step definitions''' (<code>src/test/java/imdbTests</code>) map each step to code. <code>Hooks</code> takes a screenshot when a scenario fails and always closes the browser.
* '''Page objects''' (<code>src/test/java/pageObjects</code>): <code>TopRatedPage</code>, <code>GenreSearchResultsPage</code>, <code>TitlePage</code> and <code>SignInPage</code> hold all selectors. They share <code>BasePage</code>, which provides explicit waits, scrolling and clicking helpers, and IMDb bot-protection handling.
* '''Managers''' (<code>src/test/java/managers</code>) start and stop the browser and create page objects. '''Configuration''' comes from <code>configuration.properties</code>, and any value can be overridden with <code>-D</code>.
* Each scenario gets a fresh browser and starts signed out.

== IMDb bot protection ==
IMDb sometimes shows a "confirm you are human" CAPTCHA to automated browsers. The suite does '''not''' try to get around it:
* With a visible browser, it prints a message and waits (default 180 seconds) for a person to solve the CAPTCHA.
* Chrome uses its own profile folder (<code>chrome-profile/</code>, not in git) and keeps only the CAPTCHA-pass cookie between scenarios, so one solve usually lasts for the whole run and later runs.
* Headless runs can't show a CAPTCHA, and IMDb currently refuses headless browsers with "403 Forbidden". In both cases the run stops at once with an explanation.

== Running the tests ==
Requirements: JDK 17 or newer, Maven 3.9 or newer, and Google Chrome.
<pre>
cd ImdbProject/hellocucumber
mvn test
</pre>
Common options:
{| class="wikitable"
! Command !! Effect
|-
| <code>mvn test -Dbrowser=firefox</code> || Use Firefox (or <code>safari</code>)
|-
| <code>mvn test -DtitleId=tt0068646</code> || Test a different movie's page
|-
| <code>mvn test -Dheadless=true</code> || No browser window (currently blocked by IMDb)
|}
In IntelliJ, run <code>imdbTests/RunImdbTests</code>, or right-click a <code>.feature</code> file and choose ''Run''.

The report is written to <code>target/cucumber-reports/imdb.html</code>. Failed scenarios include a screenshot and the page URL.

== Current status ==
As of 10 November 2026, all 12 automated IMDb scenarios and all 8 tutorial scenarios pass against the live site; the 5 <code>@manual</code> scenarios are skipped.

